	(text "JESD204C global nets JESD_ADC_P0..15 and JESD_ADC_N0..15 leave the AD9084 STX pins toward the Versal GTM. JESD_DAC_P/N0..15 are the SRX pins. Lane-to-ball assignment is a constraint file written against Rev D and the Versal package, after the channel-loss simulation. Line rate up to 28.21 Gbit/s NRZ. Unused STX/SRX lanes are terminated per UG-2300."
		(at 20.00 430.00 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)))
		(uuid "cc715763-988c-5dba-b321-008d1e702f92")
	)
	(text "Power domains stay split by ferrite or by their own regulator, per Rev D Table 3. AVDD1P0_CK is post-regulated by an LT3045. AVDD1P0_ADCBK is the multi-amp rail and is a Silent Switcher module, not an LDO. SERDES voltage is whatever Rev D Table 3 specifies for the JESD supply; the net name P0V9_SERDES is the contract, the number is confirmed from that table before the PCB is taped out."
		(at 20.00 450.00 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)))
		(uuid "98823cc5-d6db-5325-a855-6e8b16c04cf2")
	)
